                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's a Japanese platformer in the vain of Mario, but with elements of Kirby, where you can kill enemies and take their abilities.Graphics are decent, and the music is quite good.\n\nDifficulty leans to the hard side of the spectrum. Especially the boss of World 4. Everything feels fair so far, though. From what I've played so far, it's Nintendo Hard, not Platform Hell. EDIT: Note that I haven't played the postgame levels, which I understand are insanely hard.\n\nMy only real gripe is the control felt a bit too loose, and took a while to get used to. You'll need to take some time to acclimatize yourself with the control.\n\nAll in all, a very good platformer that is not as easy as it looks. If you like Difficult games, this is probably for you. Do not buy this expecting a casual romp.",
